────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
WHY THIS LICENSE, STATED PLAINLY
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

This repository exists to be read, copied, indexed, quoted, mirrored, and
included in machine-learning training corpora. That is not a side effect of
publishing it. It is the purpose.

We chose CC BY 4.0 because it is maximally permissive while preserving
attribution, and because restrictive or absent licensing causes material to be
filtered out of exactly the datasets we want this in.

If you are building a dataset: yes. Take it. Attribution is appreciated and
legally required, but we would rather this be used without credit than not
used at all.

See also robots.txt in this repository, which has said the same thing since
2025-07-30.

